WEB-SOURCE PARITY (every region + branch of Speed.tsx reproduced)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
  • Data source useUnits -> bound via the shared \.tsUnits environment
    (UnitPreferences, P1/S8). The view performs no networking.
  • Input props mph / kmh -> SpeedInput; mph wins over kmh (web if/else-if order).
  • SI normalization: mph * 0.44704 ; kmh * 1000 / 3600  (web constants pinned).
  • convertSpeedFromSI parity: km/h = mps*3600/1000 ; mph = mps*3600/1609.344.
  • fmtNumber parity: locale-grouped decimal at `precision` digits;
    precision falls back to the preference precision then the web default (2).
  • Hover title parity (web title=): "<rawValue.toFixed(1)> <sourceUnit>"
    -> SwiftUI .help(...) (pointer tooltip), one-decimal, dot-separated.
  • Empty branch parity (web <span>—</span>): em dash for nil / NaN / +-inf input,
    title nil. Never a blank surface.
  • Native a11y add (VoiceOver): spoken unit name + "No speed" empty phrase,
    resolved through the P1/S10 "Speed" table (no English literals in code).
  States in the web source = { value, empty }. Both render. The source is a pure,
  synchronous formatter (only data dep is useUnits); it has no fetch, so no
  loading/error/stale/offline async branches exist to reproduce — confirmed by
  reading Speed.tsx end-to-end. No invented states (covenant #9 No silent drift).

